{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JnvzLKijvBAy6LE6f7R8B3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd102-tsort\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/tsort: Topological Sort\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships tsort but the GNU version has consistent error formatting. The Go\n6\t  implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtsort, installed by\n7\t  coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n8\t\n9\tgoals:\n10\t  - G1: Perform a topological sort on a set of partial orderings.\n11\t  - G2: Detect and report cycles.\n12\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gtsort via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: Topological sorting\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must read pairs of strings from stdin (or FILE argument), where each pair \"A B\" means A must come before B, and produce a topological ordering on stdout, one item per line.\n20\t      - R1.2:\n21\t          text: When a cycle is detected, must print a cycle diagnostic to stderr and continue sorting the remaining items. Must exit 1 when any cycle is found.\n22\t      - R1.3:\n23\t          text: Must exit 1 when the input has an odd number of tokens (incomplete pair).\n24\t      - R1.4:\n25\t          text: Must read from FILE when given as argument, or stdin when no argument or \"-\" is given.\n26\t\n27\t  R2:\n28\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n29\t    items:\n30\t      - R2.1:\n31\t          text: Must exit 0 when sorting completes with no cycles.\n32\t      - R2.2:\n33\t          text: Must exit 1 when any cycle is detected or input is malformed.\n34\t      - R2.3:\n35\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n36\t\n37\tnon_goals:\n38\t  - cmd/tsort does not implement graphical cycle visualization.\n39\t\n40\tacceptance_criteria:\n41\t  - id: AC1\n42\t    criterion: \"echo 'a b b c' | tsort produces a, b, c in order, matching gtsort.\"\n43\t    traces:\n44\t      - R1.1\n45\t      - R1.4\n46\t  - id: AC2\n47\t    criterion: \"tsort detects a cycle and exits 1, matching gtsort.\"\n48\t    traces:\n49\t      - R1.2\n50\t  - id: AC3\n51\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtsort passes.\"\n52\t    traces:\n53\t      - R1.1\n54\t      - R1.2\n55\t  - id: AC4\n56\t    criterion: \"cmd/tsort compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n57\t    traces:\n58\t      - R1.1\n59\t      - R1.2\n60\t      - R1.3\n61\t      - R1.4\n62\t      - R2.1\n63\t      - R2.2\n64\t      - R2.3\n65\t\n66\tpackage_contract:\n67\t  imports:\n68\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eefb287e-e400-448f-ab78-fb5d1f88b05d","uuid":"ffe92544-7d66-417a-97b6-e4b965ad17b5","timestamp":"2026-05-28T16:12:59.246Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5625/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd102-tsort.yaml","content":"id: srd102-tsort\ntitle: \"cmd/tsort: Topological Sort\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships tsort but the GNU version has consistent error formatting. The Go\n  implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtsort, installed by\n  coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Perform a topological sort on a set of partial orderings.\n  - G2: Detect and report cycles.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gtsort via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Topological sorting\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must read pairs of strings from stdin (or FILE argument), where each pair \"A B\" means A must come before B, and produce a topological ordering on stdout, one item per line.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When a cycle is detected, must print a cycle diagnostic to stderr and continue sorting the remaining items. Must exit 1 when any cycle is found.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must exit 1 when the input has an odd number of tokens (incomplete pair).\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must read from FILE when given as argument, or stdin when no argument or \"-\" is given.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when sorting completes with no cycles.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any cycle is detected or input is malformed.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/tsort does not implement graphical cycle visualization.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"echo 'a b b c' | tsort produces a, b, c in order, matching gtsort.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"tsort detects a cycle and exits 1, matching gtsort.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gtsort passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/tsort compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
