{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) is requesting implementation of task #5625: a stitch task to extend cmd/tsort with requirements R1.2, R1.3, and R1.4 from srd102-tsort.yaml. The task is on branch `task/generation-run44-5625`. The task description says to modify `cmd/tsort/main.go` which should already contain implementations for R1.1 and R2.1, but the file was found to NOT exist. The full tsort utility needs to be created from scratch implementing all requirements.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Topological sort algorithm (Kahn's algorithm or DFS-based) for directed acyclic graphs\n   - Cycle detection in directed graphs with diagnostic output to stderr\n   - Reading pairs of tokens from stdin or a file argument\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing pattern against `gtsort` (GNU tsort from Homebrew coreutils)\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for cycles or malformed input\n   - The go-unix-utils project's cobbler-scaffold pipeline (measure + stitch cycles)\n   - Go module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd102-tsort.yaml` (READ - exists)\n     - Contains all requirements for tsort implementation\n     - Key requirements:\n       - R1.1: Read pairs \"A B\" (A before B), produce topological ordering on stdout, one item per line\n       - R1.2: Cycle detection → print diagnostic to stderr, continue sorting remaining items, exit 1\n       - R1.3: Odd number of tokens (incomplete pair) → exit 1\n       - R1.4: Read from FILE argument, or stdin when no argument or \"-\"\n       - R2.1: Exit 0 on no cycles\n       - R2.2: Exit 1 on cycle or malformed input\n       - R2.3: SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n     - Non-goals: No graphical cycle visualization\n\n   - `cmd/tsort/main.go` (READ ATTEMPTED - FILE DOES NOT EXIST)\n     - Task says to \"modify\" this file extending existing R1.1/R2.1 implementation\n     - File does not exist; must be created from scratch with all requirements\n\n   - `cmd/tsort/tsort_test.go` (EXISTS per repository file listing but NOT read)\n     - Listed in the repository files, contents unknown\n     - Would need to be read to understand test expectations\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (referenced in shared_protocols)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` function\n     - Signature: `func InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n     - Must be called at start of main()\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `cmd/tsort/main.go` does not exist despite the task description saying to \"modify\" it with existing R1.1/R2.1 code. This means the entire file must be created from scratch implementing ALL requirements (R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3), not just R1.2-R1.4.\n   - No user feedback received yet on any errors.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Discovered that `cmd/tsort/main.go` doesn't exist, so need to create it from scratch rather than extending existing code. This is consistent with the CLAUDE.md note: \"When this repository is in a generation run, cmd/ directories may be empty (source code is deleted and regenerated).\"\n   - Need to implement a complete topological sort with: input parsing (pairs from file/stdin), graph construction, Kahn's algorithm (or DFS), cycle detection with stderr reporting, odd-token-count validation, and proper exit codes.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive task prompt containing: role definition, repository files listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, package contracts, and constraints.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/tsort/main.go` implementing ALL tsort requirements (R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n   - Read `cmd/tsort/tsort_test.go` to understand existing test expectations\n   - Verify compilation: `go build -o bin/tsort ./cmd/tsort/`\n   - Verify vet: `go vet ./cmd/tsort/`\n   - Run tests: `go test ./cmd/tsort/... -count=1`\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria (AC1-AC3)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed reading the SRD (`srd102-tsort.yaml`) and attempted to read the existing `cmd/tsort/main.go`. The SRD read was successful and gave me all requirement details. The main.go read failed because the file doesn't exist. I was about to plan and implement the full tsort utility.\n\n   The acceptance criteria from the task are:\n   - AC1: `go build -o bin/tsort ./cmd/tsort/` compiles without errors\n   - AC2: `go vet ./cmd/tsort/` reports no issues\n   - AC3: All behaviors specified in srd102-tsort R1.2, R1.3, R1.4 are implemented\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read `cmd/tsort/tsort_test.go` to understand what tests already exist and their expectations, then create `cmd/tsort/main.go` with the complete tsort implementation covering all requirements. The implementation needs:\n   - Copyright header\n   - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` call\n   - Token parsing from stdin or FILE argument (R1.4)\n   - Odd token count validation with exit 1 (R1.3)\n   - Graph construction from pairs (R1.1)\n   - Topological sort with cycle detection (R1.1, R1.2)\n   - Cycle diagnostic to stderr, continue sorting (R1.2)\n   - Exit 0 on success, exit 1 on any cycle or malformed input (R2.1, R2.2)\n\n   Per the task: \"Implement srd102-tsort requirement R1.2 as specified in the SRD\", \"Implement srd102-tsort requirement R1.3\", \"Implement srd102-tsort requirement R1.4\". Design decision D1: \"Extend the existing cmd/tsort/main.go